# AGENTS.md — todo-cli

`todo-cli` is a Python CLI for managing local todo items. This is the
canonical agent-facing entry file; keep `CLAUDE.md` or client-specific rules
as thin mirrors only when a tool still needs them.

## Commands
- Quick test: `pytest tests/test_storage.py`
- Full test: `pytest`
- Lint and format gate: `pre-commit run --all-files`

## Repository Layout
- `todo/` — production CLI code; public behavior starts in `todo/__main__.py`.
- `tests/` — pytest suite; add or update a matching test for every behavior change.
- `scripts/`, `deploy/`, `.env*` — danger zones; do not edit without an explicit task.

## Agent Rules
- Before editing `todo/<name>.py`, read `tests/test_<name>.py` when it exists.
- Never invent dependency names; use the pinned versions in `pyproject.toml`.
- Every new public function gets a docstring and a test.

